+### Confirmed on a Redmi Note 13 (Snapdragon 685, Cortex-A73/A53)
+
+A second report has the same shape: Adreno 610 selected, the arm64 client exits with 132 within a
+second of `starting the Steam client`. Its CPU `Features` list is
+`fp asimd evtstrm aes pmull sha1 sha2 crc32 cpuid`: no `atomics`. Disassembling the arm64 client
+(`steam_client_steamdeck_publicbeta_linuxarm64` 1793740892) shows why it cannot start there:
+`libtier0_s.so`'s `ThreadInterlockedIncrement` is `ldaddal` and `ThreadInterlockedCompareExchange` is
+`casal`, with no HWCAP check before them; `steamclient.so` has 5888 such LSE instructions and
+`steamui.so` 4470. The same holds for every arm64 Proton: Proton's `Makefile.in` builds aarch64 with
+`-march=armv8.2-a`, and GE-Proton11-7-aarch64's `wineserver` (`casal` in `get_shm`), `ntdll.so`,
+`ntdll.dll` and DXVK's `d3d11.dll` carry unguarded LSE atomics. DroidDeck's own ARM64 binaries use
+outline atomics and run on ARMv8.0; FEX-2610 requires only ARMv8.0 with FP and CRC32.
+
+So on a CPU whose kernel reports no `atomics` (`CpuFeatures`, from `HWCAP_ATOMICS` in
+`/proc/self/auxv`, then `/proc/cpuinfo`):
+
+- the x86-64 client is always used, and the client choice offers only it, with the reason;
+- the x86-64 client bridges no arm64 Proton and writes `droiddeck-proton-x64`, which starts Valve's
+  x86-64 Proton under FEX without the Steam Linux Runtime container (proot gives it no namespaces, the
+  reason Linux games already use `droiddeck-direct`); it becomes the default and Proton Experimental is
+  requested when none is installed;
+- the session skips the GE-Proton aarch64 download and the arm64 client update it cannot use.
+
+Absent or unreadable feature data keeps every previous behaviour. Not yet verified on the device.
+
